# =============================================================================
# Reviewed containment claims FoodOn cannot make   (18)
# =============================================================================
# FoodOn parents processed ingredients by function -- `tahini is_a
# condiment`, `casein is_a protein extract` -- and asserts no source. These
# are the cases where the containment is real and the ontology simply has no
# axiom for it.


### butterscotch chip (artificially-flavored)  --RO:0001000-->  milk
#   evidence:   dairy-free butterscotch chips exist and are the exception; which one is in the jar is a product-label fact this layer cannot carry
#   confidence: medium
#   claim:      contains
#   query:      Milk
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   Butterscotch is brown sugar and BUTTER, and the mainstream chips -- Toll
#   House, Hershey -- list milk or milkfat and carry a milk allergen
#   declaration. FoodOn asserts no dairy for the class, so a dairy query
#   reached nothing. `(artificially-flavored)` qualifies the FLAVOUR, not the
#   fat: an artificial butterscotch flavour is routinely carried in a product
#   that still contains milk solids.
obo:FOODON_03302602 rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom obo:UBERON_0001913 ] .
local:patch-95e4ddac2a4e a local:Patch ;
    local:patchSection "contains" ;
    local:patchTarget obo:FOODON_03302602 ;
    local:patchProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    local:patchValue obo:UBERON_0001913 ;
    local:patchEvidence "dairy-free butterscotch chips exist and are the exception; which one is in the jar is a product-label fact this layer cannot carry" ;
    local:patchConfidence "medium" ;
    local:patchClaim "contains" ;
    local:patchQuery "Milk" ;
    rdfs:comment "Butterscotch is brown sugar and BUTTER, and the mainstream chips -- Toll House, Hershey -- list milk or milkfat and carry a milk allergen declaration. FoodOn asserts no dairy for the class, so a dairy query reached nothing. `(artificially-flavored)` qualifies the FLAVOUR, not the fat: an artificial butterscotch flavour is routinely carried in a product that still contains milk solids." ;
    dcterms:creator "Matt" ;
    dcterms:created "2026-09-10"^^xsd:date .

