### rye bread food product  --RO:0001000-->  rye plant
#   evidence:   FoodOn asserts no source on the class; the variants beneath it are all reached through the rye plant
#   confidence: high
#   claim:      contains
#   query:      rye plant
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   `rye bread food product` carries no derives-from at all, so a gluten query
#   reached every rye bread VARIANT (raisin rye, whole grain rye, rye bread
#   (enriched)) and not the product class itself. The label-convention repair
#   pass could not see it because the convention it follows is `<X> food
#   product -> <X> plant` and the source here is named `rye`, not `rye bread`.
obo:FOODON_00002214 rdfs:subClassOf [
    a owl:Restriction ;
    owl:onProperty obo:RO_0001000 ;
    owl:someValuesFrom obo:FOODON_03411313 ] .
