### citric acid  --sharesCompoundWith-->  grapefruit food product
#   evidence:   citrus intolerance is commonly a response to the acid rather than to the fruit proteins; the additive (E330) delivers it without any citrus in the product
#   confidence: medium
#   claim:      shared_compound
#   query:      Citrus
#   reviewer:   Matt
#   the acid citrus is named for, and the usual trigger in citrus intolerance.
#   Commercial citric acid is Aspergillus niger fermentation, not citrus, so
#   this is not a derivation -- it is the same molecule from a different
#   origin
obo:CHEBI_30769 local:sharesCompoundWith obo:FOODON_00001929 .
